.TH BASIC 1
.SH NAME
basic \- run a system BASIC source program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B basic
[--check] [--graphics=auto|off|on] file.bas
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the terminal BASIC dialect shared by Riplix and Fuse-X.
Names ignore case. Strings have dollar-suffixed names; numbers use binary64.
The interpreter supports structured conditions, loops, scoped labels, SUB/CALL,
terminal input/output and sequential text files.
.PP
--check validates statements without executing program I/O.
Graphics support is not implemented in this build; GRAPHICSAVAILABLE() is zero.
--graphics=on exits with an explanatory error.
.PP
Open a .bas file in Rift and press F5 to save and run it.
.SH FILES
/usr/share/basic/hello.bas
.br
/usr/share/basic/granny.bas
.PP
Granny Bingo uses name.sav text saves in the current directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for successful completion, 1 for program or I/O errors, 2 for command-line errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
rift(1)
